  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Music of the Umbundu-speaking Ovimbundu of Angola's Central Highlands around Huambo and Bié, documented in Ulrich Martini's 1971-72 recordings: songs with lamellophone and pieces on the ground bow and the scraped bow. The Congolese lukembi card stands in for the Ovimbundu lamellophone and the chizambi card for the scraped bow.",
